Z||000000||ThatRickGuy||08-17-2000||10:37 AM||||Has anyone heard of a product called Restore 4? (www.restore4.com) I saw an infomertial on it a few days ago and they showed a man cleaning up a fiberglass boat with it. I was just wondering if it would help clean up the white sun burn marks on my hood and spoiler. Or if theres any other products out there people have found to be good. BTW my engine is on it's way to the shop for the 3.1 crank, bore and balance as soon as I can find a way to haul it up there.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Old Lar||08-17-2000||11:24 AM||||The white sun burn on your car is the breakdown of the clear coat and the paint underneath.  You can try about any product to see if it works.  I've used the "color wax" which does a temporary coverup of slight oxidation.  The only real fix is sandpaper and repaint.||||reg||1
